.TH "CSDLC-SPRINT" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-sprint \- inspect sprint readiness from retained issue readbacks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc sprint \-\-repo\-root ROOT \-\-request REQUEST
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Read\-only helper consumes typed retained issue readbacks, explicit membership and sequential/parallel/hybrid scheduling. It does not authenticate new remote state, bind child worktrees or launch workers. Its retained task\-artifact layout is not a substitute for native six\-card readiness of current issues.
.SH OPTIONS
\&\-\-repo\-root: Explicit repository discovery root. Required by foundation/sprint; optional for local\-family commands. It does not override authenticated binding guards.
.PP
\&\-\-request: Required path to a UTF\-8 JSON request of the command's request family.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.SH REQUEST
\&SprintReadinessRequest; see csdlc\-requests(1) and docs/csdlc\-v3/man/examples/sprint.json.
.SH EFFECTS
\&Observation or static model only. Read findings/status, not just process exit status; no release or lifecycle activation authority is granted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&csdlc sprint \-\-repo\-root . \-\-request sprint\-request.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1).
